 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls**
 *   **Grid Name Case Sensitivity:** The volume renders black or invisible if the grid name in the channel field is misspelled or has the wrong case, or if no light has volume contribution above zero [S2, unofficial][S3].
-*   **Insufficient Samples:** The volume looks noisy if light samples are insufficient. Lights dominate volume noise; scattering-heavy media need more samples than absorption-heavy ones [S2, unofficial][S3].
-*   **Low Resolution:** The volume looks blocky if simulation resolution is too low. Shader remapping can soften it, but higher resolution cache is required to truly fix it [S2, unofficial][S3].
-*   **VRAM Limits:** The render aborts with an out of VRAM error if the VDB does not fit in GPU memory. Volumes are excluded from out-of-core systems [S2, unofficial][S3].
-*   **Flat Clouds:** The cloud looks flat or grey if Volume Trace Depth is too low. Fix by raising depth with Brute Force GI, keeping Extinction Falloff at 0.2, and lowering Shadow Density Scale [S2, unofficial][S3].
-*   **Washed Out Fog:** Fog washes out the frame if Environment Scattering value is too high. Reduce drastically; even small values are powerful [S2, unofficial][S3].
-*   **Benchmark Confusion:** Do not confuse the volume shader material with 'Volume Shader BM', which is a GPU stress test benchmark, not a material [S2, unofficial][S3].
